===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|broker|lang=enm}}, {{term|brokour|lang=enm}}, {{term|brocour|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno}} {{term|brocour||small trader|lang=xno}} (compare also {{term|abroker||to act as a broker|lang=xno}}), from {{etyl|odt}} *{{term||brokere|one who determines the usages of trade, manager|lang=odt}}, from {{term|broke|lang=odt}}, {{term|bruyck|lang=odt}}, {{term|breuck||use, usage, trade|lang=odt}}, from {{proto|Germanic|brūkiz|use, custom|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bhrug-|to use, enjoy|lang=en}}, equivalent to {{suffix|brook|er}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|brukere||a broker|lang=gml}}, {{etyl|frs|-}} {{term|broker||a broker|lang=frs}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|bruger||a broker, user, handler|lang=da}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|bruk||use, custom, trade, business|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|broc||use, profit, advantage, foredeal|lang=ang}}. Compare also {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|brocanter||to deal in second-hand goods|lang=fr}} from the same {{etyl|gem}} source. More at {{l|en|brook}}.

